import sys
p = sys.argv[1]
lines = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\n')
idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| 689 |')]
assert len(idx) == 1
rows = [
"| 690 | 2026-10-27 | **The Workbooks for the Grade 4 rooms (Build AX).** As Build AN made them for Grades 2-3: one page facing each Lesson Book step (try it with an example, at home this week, play), then the check-up on paper (four parts of four marks, pass 3+), and the teacher's copy gains every answer and the scoring. Scales and Arpeggios, Grade 4: which note finger 4 plays in every octave; the beat notes of a scale four to a beat; mirror twins in the Grade 4 contrary-motion keys; both hands' chromatic fingers; arpeggio fingers. Keys and Intervals, Grade 4: name the key from its signature; the raised 7th written with the right letter; diatonic or chromatic semitones; intervals above and below the tonic, and inversions; where a tune modulates; transposing a melody onto an empty staff. Chords and Cadences, Grade 4: name chords in root position and first inversion; the four cadences; a chord under every note of a melody (K4Melody draws an empty box under a note for '_'). Rhythm, Grade 4: counts under syncopation, hemiola, 6/4 and 12/8; bar lines for a phrase. Hear and Sing, Grade 4 has no Workbook (all by ear), as Hear and Sing Further. Every answer is computed from the room's data. The harmony teacher's copy, page 5, now lists the chords (it listed only the melody notes). Every page checked for overflow. Source patch717.py; tests ax717.js, axdata.js. |",
"| 691 | 2026-10-27 | **A melody for a couplet, a Grade 4 lesson in the Melody room (Build AY; Theory of Music Grade 4).** After Writing a melody, marked Grade 4: the couplet's words set the rhythm the way Words and rhythm does (a bar line before each strong syllable, an anacrusis when a line starts weak), the child writes a note for every syllable in C, G, D, F or B♭ major or A, E, B, D or G minor (harmonic: the 7th raised, its sharp drawn once a bar), the words sit under the notes, line 1 ends away from the tonic and line 2 on it, a phrase mark over each line; five points tick as you go; an example for every couplet in every key. MwStaff learns any number of bars in lines, words under the notes, phrase marks by note, the raised 7th; Writing a melody draws as before. Not a Lesson Book page yet (the chapter's pages, Workbook and checks stay as they are): it can become step 8 with a Workbook page if she wants it there. Source patch718.py; tests ay718.js, ay718b.js (EN/KO, desktop and phone, every example keeps all five points, 0 errors), chsweep 42 chapters 0 errors, booksweep 0 errors, regression 300 lessons, 50 drills, 0 errors. Local commit only, not pushed. |",
]
for r in reversed(rows): lines.insert(idx[0] + 1, r)
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(lines)); print('ok')
